---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Process — Dhyai"
  description="From drawing to block carving to hand printing — the Dhyai process prioritises structure and surface clarity at every step."
  ogImage="/assets/images/process_block_print.jpg"
  ogUrl="/process.html"
  currentPage="process"
>

  <!-- ══ Hero ══ -->
  <div class="page-hero">
    <img
      src="/assets/images/process_block_print.jpg"
      alt="Block printing at the Dhyai studio"
      loading="eager"
      fetchpriority="high"
    >
    <div class="page-hero-overlay"></div>
  </div>

  <!-- ══ Intro ══ -->
  <section class="section reveal">
    <span class="kicker" style="margin-bottom:1.2rem">The Process</span>
    <div class="rule-h"></div>
    <h1 style="font-size:clamp(2.5rem,6vw,5rem); letter-spacing:.2em; margin-bottom:2rem">Process</h1>
    <p style="max-width:560px; margin-bottom:1.2rem">
      Material selection is directed by structure and surface clarity.
      Drawing establishes scale. Blocks are carved to preserve alignment.
      Printing is executed by hand. Each study is reviewed in light before release.
    </p>
    <p style="max-width:560px">
      Engraving follows defined measurement. Surface application is controlled and restrained.
      Nothing is released until the surface holds.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- ══ Process steps ══ -->
  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="process-grid reveal">
      <div class="process-step">
        <img src="/assets/images/process_drawing.jpg" alt="Drawing — establishing scale and proportion" loading="lazy">
        <p class="process-step-num">01 · Drawing</p>
        <p>Scale and rhythm are resolved on paper first. The composition must hold before the block is made.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="process-step d1">
        <img src="/assets/images/process_block_detail.jpg" alt="Block carving — precision alignment" loading="lazy">
        <p class="process-step-num">02 · Block carving</p>
        <p>Blocks are carved by hand to preserve alignment. Tolerance is measured, not estimated.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="process-step d2">
        <img src="/assets/images/process_printing_hand.jpg" alt="Hand printing — measured application" loading="lazy">
        <p class="process-step-num">03 · Printing</p>
        <p>Each impression is placed by hand. Pressure and pace are consistent across the surface.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="process-step d3">
        <img src="/assets/images/material_surface_close.jpg" alt="Surface review — assessed in light" loading="lazy">
        <p class="process-step-num">04 · Review</p>
        <p>Finished surfaces are assessed in natural light. Only pieces that hold their structure are released.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══ Material section ══ -->
  <section class="section" style="border-top:1px solid rgba(237,227,204,.05)">
    <div class="two-col reveal">
      <div class="two-col-img">
        <img
          src="/assets/images/material_surface_close.jpg"
          alt="Cotton surface — selected for printing response"
          loading="lazy"
        >
      </div>
      <div class="two-col-text">
        <span class="kicker">Material</span>
        <div class="rule-h"></div>
        <h2>Cotton selected for surface clarity</h2>
        <p>
          Weight and weave are matched to each study before production begins.
          The cloth must receive the block cleanly — no bleed, no slip.
        </p>
        <p>
          Mulmul for dohars. Slub cotton for bedcovers.
          Each format uses the material best suited to how it will be used.
        </p>
        <p>
          The surface improves with washing. Softening, not wearing.
        </p>
        <a href="/contact.html" class="btn-enquire">Enquire about a piece</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══ Process brief ══ -->
  <section class="section" style="border-top:1px solid rgba(237,227,204,.05); text-align:center">
    <div class="statement reveal">
      <span class="kicker" style="margin-bottom:2rem">In summary</span>
      <div class="rule" style="margin-bottom:3rem"></div>
      <p style="max-width:560px; margin:0 auto 1rem">Material selection is directed by structure and surface clarity.</p>
      <p style="max-width:560px; margin:0 auto 1rem">Drawing establishes scale. Blocks are carved to preserve alignment.</p>
      <p style="max-width:560px; margin:0 auto 1rem">Printing is executed by hand. Engraving follows defined measurement.</p>
      <p style="max-width:560px; margin:0 auto">Surface application is controlled and restrained. Each study is reviewed in light before release.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
